From 4d4940ad9d90a03975e28ec349174ac5163a1cca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:12:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 065/115] power: supply: qcom_smbx: don't zero USBIN
 voltage/current when full

smb_get_iio_chan() backs both POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW and
POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW for the USB power supply, and only reads
the IIO channel when POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS reads back
POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING; otherwise it reports 0.

That is wrong once the battery reaches float and BATTERY_CHARGER_STATUS_1
moves to TERMINATE_CHARGE or INHIBIT_CHARGE, which smb_get_prop_status()
correctly maps to POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL rather than CHARGING. With a
live supply still attached, USBIN is still powered and the ADC channels
still read real values, but the status gate forces both to 0. Userspace
sees a fully charged battery on AC report 0 V / 0 A input, which looks
like the charger was unplugged.

Gate on whether USBIN is actually the active input power source instead
(the same POWER_PATH_STATUS check smb_get_prop_usb_online() already
uses), not on whether the battery happens to be mid-charge. This is true
whenever a cable is delivering power, full battery or not, and false
when there's genuinely nothing connected -- the case the 0 V / 0 A
fallback exists for.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index b1cb925581ec..8f3f0fc42281 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -599,12 +599,10 @@ static void smb_status_change_work(struct work_struct *work)
 static int smb_get_iio_chan(struct smb_chip *chip, struct iio_channel *chan,
 			     int *val)
 {
-	int rc;
-	union power_supply_propval status;
+	int rc, usb_online = 0;
 
-	rc = power_supply_get_property(chip->chg_psy, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS,
-				       &status);
-	if (rc < 0 || status.intval != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING) {
+	rc = smb_get_prop_usb_online(chip, &usb_online);
+	if (rc < 0 || !usb_online) {
 		*val = 0;
 		return 0;
 	}
